{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Twenty-two thousand.</b> We have already said that since they are the camp of the Shekhinah, and the Shekhinah does not rest on fewer than twenty-two thousand, therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, diminished them and established them at this number, to indicate that the camp of the Shekhinah is no less than twenty-two thousand. And the Ramban wrote that because they were not included in the affliction of Egypt, therefore they were not included in the multiplicity, for everyone who was included in ״פֶּן יִרְבֶּה״ was in the blessing of ״כֵּן יִרְבֶּה״. Although this is the way of derash, nevertheless it appears one may add to it an explanation, for HaShem did not multiply them against nature except in order to frustrate the counsel of the nations who sought to diminish them through affliction, and HaShem wanted to deny them everything that they plotted to do — and on the contrary, He multiplied them beyond nature, for they bore six in one womb. But the tribe of Levi, who was not included in the affliction, therefore had no need to be multiplied against nature, and they were fruitful and multiplied in the manner of all the world. And this is indeed a sound reason, and it may be that this is the opinion of the Ramban. And some say that they were not multiplied so that it would be easy for Israel to provide for them. And this is a far-fetched reason, for there is no hindrance to HaShem to save and sustain His servants who do His will. And some say that the Ark consumed them, and this is the Ark of Jacob, and this is the opinion of the Ramban that we cited, as explained above in the portion of וַיֵּצֵא (Genesis 29:34) on the verse ״עַל כֵּן קָרָא שְׁמוֹ לֵוִי״. And some say that the Holy One, blessed be He, foresaw that they would not all be righteous, therefore He removed many of them from the world and there remained a kav and clean, so that all who were occupied with the Ark would be righteous. And this is what they said, that the Ark consumed them." "And it appears to me, since we find regarding Pharaoh's decree that Amram divorced his wife and remained a long time without procreation and multiplication — for Yocheved was 130 years old when he married her a second time — and what our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Sotah 12a), 'They all arose and divorced their wives,' presumably not all Israel did so, for how could they have remained a long time without a wife? For our Rabbis of blessed memory said there (Sotah 11b) that in the merit of righteous women our forefathers were redeemed, etc., and it concludes there with all the kindnesses they did for their husbands when they were in crushing labor — hear from this that the husbands could not have held out without the women. And it further concludes there that they were fruitful and multiplied in the field — hear from this that even at the time of the decree they did not divorce their wives. Rather, certainly what it concludes, 'they all arose and divorced their wives,' means all the sons of the tribe of Levi, who were not included in the enslavement; nevertheless they feared the decree of ״כָּל הַבֵּן הַיִּלוֹד הַיְאֹרָה תַּשְׁלִיכֻהוּ״, for on a single day he commanded this even upon the children of the Egyptians — therefore they too feared lest this cup pass over them, and the majority of the tribe of Levi stood a long time without women, just as Amram stood a long time without a wife. And therefore the tribe of Levi was few in number. And this is a sound reason, and it sits better on the heart than all the others. And HaShem chose them precisely because they were few, for so we find in many places that the Holy One, blessed be He, chooses the few, as it is written (Deuteronomy 7:7): ״לֹא מֵרֻבְּכֶם וגו׳ כִּי אַתֶּם הַמְעַט״. And likewise among these three families, Gershon, Kehath, and Merari, Merari was the most populous, therefore he was distanced from the burden of the holy and it was given to the fewer. And this matter is self-evident."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:39:38.654042093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}